flow "Temporal workflow replay"
summary "A worker crashes mid-workflow and another resumes by replaying event history."
tags workflows durable-execution fault-tolerance
level intermediate
source "https://docs.temporal.io/workflow-execution"
related distributed-systems/saga-compensation

group temporal "Temporal cluster"
node starter "Client" actor
node server "Temporal Server" service in=temporal
node history "Event History" db in=temporal
node worker-a "Worker A" service
node worker-b "Worker B" service hidden
edge starter > server
edge server > history
edge server > worker-a
edge server > worker-b hidden
edge history > worker-b dashed hidden
array events "History" orientation=column = Started

scenario crash "Worker crashes, workflow resumes"
  step start "Start workflow"
    "The client starts a workflow. The server records a `WorkflowStarted` event and hands a task to Worker A."
    send starter > server "start"
    send server > history "Started"
    send server > worker-a "task"
  step activity "Activity completes"
    "Worker A runs the workflow code, which schedules an activity. The result is **appended** to history before the workflow moves on."
    state worker-a active
    send worker-a > server "ChargeCard done"
    values events = Started "ChargeCard done"
  step crash-a "Worker A crashes"
    "Worker A dies mid-workflow. It held local variables, but they do not matter: history is the source of truth, not worker memory."
    state worker-a error
    callout worker-a "Local state lost"
  step takeover "Worker B takes over"
    "The server times out Worker A's task and schedules it on Worker B, which has never seen this workflow."
    show worker-b,server-worker-b
    send server > worker-b "task"
  step replay "Replay history"
    "Worker B **replays** the workflow code against the recorded events. `ChargeCard` is not run again; its recorded result is returned instead."
    detail "During replay, the Worker verifies that every Command emitted by workflow code matches Event History; any divergence (from `time.Now()`, direct I/O, or unversioned code edits) triggers a non-determinism error. Normally, **Sticky Execution** keeps state in an in-memory LRU **Workflow Cache** so full replay runs only on crash or cache eviction."
    show history-worker-b
    send history > worker-b "events"
    state events#0..1 success
    state worker-b active
  step resume "Continue where it stopped"
    "Replay catches Worker B up to the crash point, and then it executes new work, appending to the same history."
    detail "A single Workflow Run has a default hard limit of **51,200 events** (or **50 MB**, warning at 10,240 events). Long-running loops use **Continue-As-New** to close the current run and start a fresh Event History under the same Workflow ID."
    values events = Started "ChargeCard done" "ShipOrder done"
    state worker-b success
